{"disposition":"Admissible disclosures and inconsistency follow-up evidence policy","quote":"1.\n\nAre intermediaries required to obtain documentary evidence to support\ninformation provided by a client in assessing whether the client qualifies as a\nsophisticated professional investor (“SPI”)?\nIntermediaries should be satisfied that a client has met the qualifying criteria of an SPI\nbefore treating the client as such. Where an intermediary has made reasonable efforts\nto obtain information from a client during the know-your-client process, the intermediary\nmay rely on the information disclosed by the client to ascertain whether the client could\nqualify as an SPI. The intermediary should beware of any inconsistencies between the\ninformation provided and that held with the intermediary, and in such cases, clarify with\nthe client.\n\n","rule_ids":["spi.assessment"],"span_id":"spi.annex2.1"}